<VI _name="pa_reg_to_control.vi" description="Kit helper (init registration shape\3B built on pa_insert_series2.xml and pa_wire_dyn_deep.xml\3B measured 2026-10). In a helper-loop VI it replaces the top-level Register For Events by an INPUT CONTROL that carries the same event registration refnum: (1) Create Control on Register's input 'event registration refnum' (typed like the registration), (2) remembers the far end of Register's refnum output wire (the loop tunnel) and the owners of the sources on 'event source' (Unbundle By Name) and 'error in (no error)' (the fresh no-error constant), (3) deletes every wire on Register and on that Unbundle, (4) deletes Register, the Unbundle and the constant, (5) wires the new control's terminal to the remembered far end, (6) assigns the control to connector pane slot 'term index' (AssignCtrlToTerm), (7) Save.Instrument. No Remove Bad Wires (it would remove the sourceless inner refnum chain before step 5). Project OPEN and ACTIVE.">
